# Auto-push completed changes

- After completing a user-requested code change and its relevant validation, commit the task-related changes and push the current branch to its configured remote.
- Include only files related to the completed request. Preserve unrelated user changes and never commit secrets, local data, generated credentials, or payment artifacts.
- Check the branch and remote before pushing. Integrate remote updates safely; never force-push unless the user explicitly requests it.
- If validation, commit, authentication, reconciliation, or push fails, report the exact blocker instead of claiming the code was uploaded.
- A code push does not authorize deployment, publication, signing, or payment.
